I find coplots a super useful visual tool for interpreting interactions in mixed models, but sometimes I'd like to also see the breakdown in numbers so that I can compare intercepts, etc and know the exact bins of the "Given" variable that R is magically choosing. Does anyone know how to extract the regression output from coplots?

for example, this code below gives me the attached plot. I'd be down to see the regression output for simple linear regressions if that's all I can get, or for the full mixed models at these different levels of the "Given" variable if possible. I realize that I could code the model for each of these different levels, but I'd rather see what the coplot is doing and have them line up exactly. And it would be faster if there is just a line of code for this. Can't find anything via google, though others have asked the question, to no avail. Let me know what you think - Thanks!

coplot(log_DEA ~ daub_veg_H1_total_veg_cover | Fore_slope_ammended, rows=1, panel=panel.car, lowess.line=FALSE, data=DEAslope)

