Hi all,
I have a list of data frames that all look like this, except the third column which has different names.
the names of the elements of the list are the header of the third column
   id area      CH4
1 132 7339 2.122865
2 131 7279 2.107544
3 130 7086 2.058260
4 129 7288 2.109842
5 128 7280 2.107799
6 127 7221 2.092733

 I want to merge the third column of all data frames in the list to another existing data frame by the "id" column.
So that I get a data frame with the first column "id" followed by "CH4"....
The left_join only works on data frames and not lists.
lapply with merge gives me a list of merged data frames

It seems like there should be an easy way but I can't find it on google or think of one.

Thanks

