Hi there,
Mike's answer is much more complete, but I use the bind_rows function often. I would use a simplified version of what Mike sent, it will include NAs for non-matches...not sure if that's what you are after. Using same example data:

library(dplyr)
df.list<-bind_rows(l) # add NAs for non-matches
df.all<-merge(df.list, target_df, by="id") # merge by "id"
head(dff)

